# ---------- Watchdog (Service Settings [7]/[8]) ----------
SVC_MENU_WDOG_ON=[7] Enable watchdog - restart winws if it crashes
SVC_MENU_WDOG_OFF=[8] Disable watchdog
WDOG_STATUS_LABEL=Watchdog:
WDOG_SERVICE_CONFLICT=The Windows service is installed. The watchdog only manages winws started by this app, so it is not enabled while the service exists.
WDOG_FAILED=Could not create the scheduled task. Make sure the app is running as administrator.
WDOG_ENABLED=Enabled. Every 2 minutes it checks winws and restarts it if it stopped unexpectedly.
WDOG_NOTE=If you press Stop, winws is not restarted until you press Start again. It gives up after 3 failed restarts in a row. Closing winws in Task Manager counts as a crash and is restarted too. Results are logged in logs\app.log.
WDOG_DISABLED=Disabled. The watchdog task was removed.
WDOG_ALREADY_OFF=The watchdog was already disabled.
WDOG_DELETE_FAILED=Could not remove the scheduled task. Run the app as administrator and try again.

